  <div class="container">
    <h1>🛡️ MEENGLE - SAFETY TIPS & BEST PRACTICES</h1>
    <p><strong>Your safety is our top priority. Follow these guidelines to have a safe and positive experience on MEENGLE.</strong></p>

    <h2>🔐 Protecting Your Account</h2>
    
    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Use a Strong, Unique Password</strong>
      <p>Create a password with at least 12 characters including uppercase, lowercase, numbers, and symbols. Don't use the same password on other websites.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Enable Two-Factor Authentication</strong>
      <p>Go to Settings → Security → Two-Factor Authentication. This adds an extra layer of protection to your account.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Never Share Your Password</strong>
      <p>MEENGLE will never ask for your password via email or message. If someone does, it's a scam. Report it immediately.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Keep Your Email Secure</strong>
      <p>Your email is tied to your MEENGLE account. Use a secure email with a strong password and two-factor authentication.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>👤 Profile & Photo Safety</h2>
    
    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Use Recent, Clear Photos</strong>
      <p>Post recent photos that clearly show your face. This helps people recognize you and builds trust.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Don't Share Identifying Information in Bio</strong>
      <p>Avoid including your full name, workplace, home address, phone number, or social media in your profile until you trust someone.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Never Post Explicit Photos</strong>
      <p>Don't share nude, semi-nude, or sexually explicit images. They can be screenshot, shared, or used for blackmail.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Be Cautious with Location Sharing</strong>
      <p>Don't share your exact location, workplace, gym, or places you frequent until you've met someone in person.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>💬 Safe Messaging Practices</h2>
    
    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Take Time Before Meeting</strong>
      <p>Message for at least a week before agreeing to meet. Get to know their personality, interests, and values.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Verify Their Story</strong>
      <p>Ask questions about their life, job, interests, and background. Look for consistency. Inconsistencies may indicate catfishing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Trust Your Instincts</strong>
      <p>If something feels off about someone—weird questions, lack of detail, rushing to meet—trust your gut. It's okay to unmatch.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Never Send Money</strong>
      <p>This is a huge red flag. Legitimate people you're dating won't ask for money. Ever. Not for flights, emergencies, or investments.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="warning-box">
      <strong>⚠️ Be Wary of These Red Flags:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>They ask for money or Bitcoin</li>
        <li>They claim to love you after knowing you a few days</li>
        <li>Their photos look like they belong to a model</li>
        <li>They only have 1-2 photos</li>
        <li>They refuse to video call before meeting</li>
        <li>They claim to be "newly in town" and don't know people</li>
        <li>They ask you to move conversations to WhatsApp/text immediately</li>
        <li>They claim to be rich/traveling/mysterious</li>
      </ul>
    </warning-box>

    <h2>🚗 Meeting in Person Safety</h2>
    
    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Always Meet in Public Places</strong>
      <p>Choose busy public places like coffee shops, restaurants, bars, or parks. Never agree to meet at their home, your home, or isolated locations on a first date.</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Tell a trusted friend where you're going and who you're meeting</li>
      <li>Share your location with a friend during the date</li>
      <li>Set up a time to text your friend when you arrive safely</li>
      <li>Plan your own transportation (drive or get your own Uber)</li>
      <li>Keep your phone charged and accessible</li>
      <li>Have a safety call setup (friend calls you after 30 mins to check in)</li>
      <li>Know how you're getting home in advance</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Do a Video Call First</strong>
      <p>Before meeting, do a video call to verify they're who they claim to be. Legitimate people will be happy to video chat.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Take Time on First Dates</strong>
      <p>Plan for a short first date (30-60 minutes). It's easier to extend if it's going well than to cut it short if it's not.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="danger-box">
      <strong>🚨 If You Feel Unsafe:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Excuse yourself to the bathroom and call a friend</li>
        <li>Leave immediately if you feel threatened</li>
        <li>Don't worry about being rude—safety comes first</li>
        <li>Tell nearby staff members if you're in danger</li>
        <li>Call police if threatened or harassed</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>🛑 Reporting & Blocking</h2>
    
    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Report Suspicious Behavior</strong>
      <p>If someone harasses, threatens, or scams you, report them immediately. Click the ⋮ menu and select "Report." Our team reviews all reports within 24 hours.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Block Users Who Make You Uncomfortable</strong>
      <p>You don't need a reason to block someone. If they weird you out, block them. They won't be able to message or see your profile.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Don't Engage with Scammers</strong>
      <p>If you suspect a scam, stop engaging. Don't argue with them. Block and report them. They're trying to manipulate you.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>💰 Financial Safety</h2>
    
    <div class="danger-box">
      <strong>🚨 NEVER:</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Send money to someone you haven't met in person</li>
        <li>Share credit card information via message</li>
        <li>Participate in "make money fast" schemes promoted by matches</li>
        <li>Invest in cryptocurrencies suggested by matches</li>
        <li>Buy gift cards at their request</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Be Cautious with Payment Information</strong>
      <p>MEENGLE's payment system is secure with Stripe. Only enter payment info on our official app/website, never via message or external links.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>🎯 General Safety Reminders</h2>
    
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Be yourself—authenticity is attractive and safe</li>
      <li>Take your time getting to know someone</li>
      <li>Trust your gut feeling about people</li>
      <li>Keep personal information private until you trust someone</li>
      <li>Don't feel obligated to respond to anyone</li>
      <li>It's okay to end conversations anytime</li>
      <li>Report anything that violates our community guidelines</li>
      <li>Remember that MEENGLE team members will never ask for passwords or personal info via message</li>
      <li>Have fun, but stay alert</li>
      <li>Dating should be enjoyable, not stressful</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>🚀 If You Encounter These Scams</h2>
    
    <div class="danger-box">
      <strong>Romance Scam:</strong> Person claims to fall in love quickly, makes excuses not to meet in person, eventually asks for money. (REPORT & BLOCK)
    </div>

    <div class="danger-box">
      <strong>Catfishing:</strong> Using fake photos or false information. Refuses video call before meeting. (REPORT & BLOCK)
    </div>

    <div class="danger-box">
      <strong>Investment Scam:</strong> Matches promote crypto, stocks, or "business opportunities" to make quick money. (REPORT & BLOCK)
    </div>

    <div class="danger-box">
      <strong>Photo Extortion:</strong> Someone asks for explicit photos, then threatens to share them unless you pay. (REPORT & CONTACT POLICE)
    </div>

    <h2>📞 Need Help?</h2>
    
    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Report Inappropriate Behavior:</strong>
      <p>Use the report feature in-app. Provide specific details and screenshots if possible.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Safety Concerns:</strong>
      <p>Email safety@meengle.com with details of the issue.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>General Support:</strong>
      <p>Email support@meengle.com for technical issues or account help.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip-box">
      <strong>Emergency:</strong>
      <p>If you're in immediate danger, call 911 (or your local emergency number) and provide police with information about the person.</p>
    </div>

    <hr style="margin: 40px 0; border: none; border-top: 2px solid #eee;">

    <p style="text-align: center; color: #667eea; font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px;">Your safety is our responsibility. Stay smart, stay safe, and have fun on MEENGLE! 💚</p>

